.TH LIBMPQ__ARCHIVE_SIGN 3 2026-09-18 "The MoPaQ archive library"
.SH NAME
libmpq__archive_sign \- configure weak signing before writer close
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <libmpq/mpq.h>

int32_t libmpq__archive_sign(mpq_archive_s *archive, uint32_t type,
    const uint8_t *private_key, size_t key_size);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Weak MPQ signatures use MD5 with RSA-512 and PKCS#1 v1.5. They are obsolete
and must not be used for modern authenticity decisions. Strong signatures
are not supported.
.PP
Each raw key is exactly 128 bytes: a 64-byte unsigned big-endian modulus
followed by a zero-padded 64-byte big-endian exponent value. Use a public key
to verify a signature and a private key to create one. The modulus must be
full-width and odd; the exponent
must be odd, at least 3, and less than the modulus. No keys or PEM parser are
built in. These checks do not establish mathematical key-pair validity.
.PP
Detection returns zero for absence or LIBMPQ_SIGNATURE_WEAK for structurally
valid storage. Verification requires exactly LIBMPQ_SIGNATURE_WEAK and a
public key. A mismatch returns success with that bit set, not a negative error.
The non-NULL output masks are zeroed before validation and remain zero on errors.
.PP
Signing requires a v1 or v2 writer with no active file writer and may be configured
only once. It immediately consumes one file slot for a zeroed 72-byte
(signature) file, copies the key, and signs at close after finalizing all tables
and internal files. Signature attribute values are zero. The retained key is
cleared on close, including failure. Reopen to verify the signed result.
.PP
Hashing starts at the MPQ archive offset and covers the declared archive extent for v1
or the metadata-derived required extent for v2,
with all 72 signature bytes treated as zero. The stored signature integer is
little-endian. The first eight bytes must be zero; compressed, encrypted,
sector-CRC, overlapping, and incorrectly sized signature storage is rejected.
Reader verification is independent of archive version and writer compression
policy. Warcraft III map-header hashing is not implemented.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Zero on success; existing negative libmpq errors on failure.
EXIST denotes NULL required handles/outputs or an absent requested signature;
FORMAT denotes malformed storage/key, unsupported flags, or unsupported
signing version; NOT_INITIALIZED denotes the wrong handle/lifecycle.
I/O and writer capacity errors are propagated.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libmpq (3),
.BR libmpq__archive_signatures (3),
.BR libmpq__archive_verify (3)
